        "sources": {
            "supplies.plus": "the battery block below",
            "battery": "per cell (6 small alkaline cells in series), Energizer/Eveready 522: rated 625 mAh at 25 mA continuous to 0.8 V per cell (Eveready 522 datasheet, average capacity). Curve: the AA alkaline shape (see battery_4xaa), 0 % = 0.8 V per cell at 25 mA; resistance ~1.7 ohm per pack fresh (estimate, the earlier model's value) rising as for the AA. Estimate: measure your battery",
            "battery.rate": "fitted with tools/fit_battery.py (the simulation's own model) to 625 mAh at 25 mA and ~450 mAh at 100 mA to 4.8 V (secondary readings of the Energizer 522 life graph: 'about 24 h at 25 mA', 'less than 5 hours at 100 mA', baldengineer.com '9V batteries suck'); rms error 4 %. Another reading (~300 mAh at 100 mA to 7 V) gives 233 mAh in the model: the mid-discharge voltage at 100 mA is probably a little low"
        }
